A||N||4||Rumor||DON'T  live in NY!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Rumor||12-27-2001||03:15 AM||||Man!<BR>  I live in Queens NY, which has a very, very high car theft rate.  I bought a grey 85 GT which had an alarm already installed.  The people around here park their cars by bumping the car behind them and in front of them. Someone was kind enouch to do that to my car this morning after I left for work, and I came home to this note on my windshield:<P>"Please shut off your alarm, it is ringing in our eyes, or fix your window. <BR>           -Neighbors"<P>Someone didn't like the fact that my alarm went off, so they smashed my passenger window.  Gotta love New York. Gotta love the "ringing in our eyes" part too.<P>*tosses up his hands*<P>So, I suppose it's off to the auto shop tomorrow to get a replacement window.<P>Anyone have any experience with this?  will an after-market window normally fit ok? <P>Or, would I be better off rummaging through a junkyard?<P>I'd be a LOT more pissed-off about it if today wasn't already a "falling-down" kind of a day. Hope everyone who reads this had a better day then I did.<P>peace.<P>-Rumor<BR>(with the all-new "black plastic bag" tinting)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||12-27-2001||04:28 AM||||did you file a police report?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||12-27-2001||07:34 AM||||The police already have a crew ready working in shifts on the case I'm sure.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>If it makes you feel any better, any Fiero passenger side window will work I believe, and they are very cheap and easy to find.  I'd file it with insurance (if possible), get their money and then go to a yard and get a cheap window.  That might even give you a little cash to buy a nice sized gun to shoot the next person who touches your car<BR>Good luck,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||kneebarx||12-27-2001||01:40 PM||||Yea, no way in hell would i Live in queens with my fiero.  I live in westchester, and although there are vandals running amok, its still not as bad as queens.  I would only park my fiero on the street there if i had a garage or something.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rumor||12-27-2001||10:09 PM||||Yea! Turns out one of my relatives owns an auto-glass place, and he was able to get the window from the junkyard - two windows for twenty bucks!  You were right about the windows being the same - the "new" window fits better then the one that was there! I have to buff out the usual vertical "slide" scratches that all old cars seem to get, but at least I have a friggin' window now.<BR>||||reg||10
